  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc. The image-only baseline was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality contributes limited signal and may benefit from reweighting rather than equal-weight concatenation. Config_033 is a direct controlled comparison to config_032, changing only fusion from concat to weighted. This isolates the fusion-strategy question: does the image branch need to be down-weighted relative to the RNA branch, or are the features complementary enough that simple concatenation suffices? Under a limited budget, this single-variable test reduces uncertainty about an important design decision (how to combine modalities) without confounding other factors (encoder, aggregation, profile setting all held constant at their best-known values). The result will directly inform whether to invest further in multimodal configurations and, if weighted fusion wins, which modality to trust more."
}

